WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.790
Meet Paramecium: a single
cell living in fresh water.

2
00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:08.140
Its cilia beat to sweep
food into a groove,

3
00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:10.860
where it is packed into a food vacuole.

4
00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:16.390
It swims away from harmful chemicals,
and expels water that enters by osmosis.

5
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.590
Then it divides in two.

6
00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.290
One cell, doing every job.

7
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:27.120
So if one cell can manage alone, why are
so many living things made of many cells?

8
00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:30.190
In this mission, you'll check
off the processes of life,

9
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.220
one by one, inside a single cell.

10
00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:37.660
Then you'll compare one-celled life
with life built from many cells.

11
00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:42.450
Your mission: explain why so many
living things are made of many cells.
